+/**
+ * ZBrush-style smooth: in addition to the regular Laplacian smoothing of the shape, every
+ * iteration also relaxes the topology (the same tangential, shape-preserving smoothing used by
+ * the Slide Relax brush). This evens out vertex distribution while the surface is smoothed,
+ * closely matching the behavior of ZBrush's Smooth brush.
+ *
+ * The value is the strength of the topology relaxation relative to the shape smoothing.
+ * 0.0 = old Blender behavior (shape only), 1.0 = full relax pass per smooth iteration.
+ */
+constexpr float topology_relax_factor = 1.0f;
